            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0089" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.8411/11–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-04T12:00:00+03:00">November 4,
                            1944—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>224. It is assumed by Ethiopian Government that as no reply has <pb facs="0090"
                        n="78" xml:id="pg78"/> been received to my telegram 214, October 24, our
                    attitude is negative and negotiations with British will proceed without
                    expectation of support hoped for.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
